    "result": "Excellent! All tests now pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. Governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- The test was importing these as named imports from the module, but they were only available in the default export\n- This fixed the \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')\" error\n\n**2. Toxicity metric interface** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n- Changed the `toxicityMetric` function signature from `(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms)`\n- This matches the interface of other metrics (`exactMatchMetric` and `lengthVarianceMetric`)\n- Previously, when called with `(outputs, references)`, the references array was being treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging outputs as toxic\n- Now it correctly uses the default banned terms and returns a score of 1 when no toxic content is detected\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests pass across all 8 test files\n\u2705 All public exports remain functional\n\u2705 No test files were modified",
